WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.7 · Internal Systems & Operations
Compliance essentials from day one

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A few protections must be in place before your first activity, registered or not.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
Compliance essentials are the few protections you need before your first activity, even before you register, if you will work with people, collect personal information, tell stories or handle money.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
The essentials to have ready

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:36.759
Code of conduct: Expected behaviour for founders, volunteers and anyone who joins. For example: Founders, mentors and trainees agree to treat customers and each other with respect.

6
00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:51.422
Safeguarding: A focal person, a reporting route and basic rules when you work with children or adults at risk. For example: The bakery names one founder as focal person and never leaves a 17-year-old alone with one adult.

7
00:00:51.422 --> 00:01:03.493
Data and consent: What personal data you collect, why and where it is kept, and consent for photos and stories. For example: The bakery asks trainees before posting any photo of them online.

8
00:01:03.493 --> 00:01:16.393
Conflicts and safety: Conflict of interest declarations, plus any safety rules or licences your activities need. For example: The bakery registers for food hygiene, and founders declare any supplier who is family.

9
00:01:16.793 --> 00:01:17.393
Why before day one

10
00:01:17.393 --> 00:01:21.956
1. Harm can happen at your very first activity.

11
00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:27.630
2. People trust you with their children, their data and their stories.

12
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:33.563
3. A missing licence or permission can stop you trading.

13
00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:34.563
What they connect to

14
00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:38.756
1. Your onboarding: every newcomer learns these essentials.

15
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:43.319
2. Your information system: data kept and accessed safely.

16
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:49.993
3. Module 10: turning them into full policies where you need them.

17
00:01:50.393 --> 00:01:50.993
What to avoid

18
00:01:50.993 --> 00:01:55.926
Waiting until you are registered to think about safeguarding.

19
00:01:55.926 --> 00:02:00.859
Long documents nobody reads instead of short, practical essentials.

20
00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:07.904
Assuming rules are the same everywhere: ask someone with a legal background.

21
00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:10.304
You list the compliance essentials your first activities need.

22
00:02:10.304 --> 00:02:14.304
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:18.904
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
